SDK 26.03 defect: std::bind moves its bound arguments and callable out on every
call (sysroot/usr/h/public/functional, Dinkum).

The identity fixer returned std::forward<_Cv_TiD>(_Tid) by value. _Cv_TiD is the
bound argument's (non-reference) type, so that is a std::move: each call moved the
bound argument out of the bind object, and a second call got a moved-from value,
e.g. an empty shared_ptr. [func.bind.bind]/10 passes bound arguments as lvalues.
_Call_binder likewise moved the stored callable (std::forward<_Cv_FD>(_Obj)).

Seen as: every rclcpp_components node executable (demo_nodes_cpp talker, listener,
...) SIGSEGVs at shutdown in rclcpp::Node::get_node_base_interface() with this ==
NULL: node_main.cpp calls the getter std::bind(&NodeT::get_node_base_interface,
node) a second time (remove_node after spin) and the bound node is gone.

Paths relative to the SDK root; applied by pkg/sdk/files/apply-sdk-patches.sh
(pkg/sdk sdk_fix, and the SDK overlay's sdk_fix_install).

--- a/vxsdk/sysroot/usr/h/public/functional
+++ b/vxsdk/sysroot/usr/h/public/functional
@@ -834,9 +834,9 @@
 	struct _Select_fixer<_Cv_TiD, false, false, 0>
 	{	// identity fixer
 	template<class _Untuple>
-		static _Cv_TiD _Fix(_Cv_TiD& _Tid, _Untuple&&)
-		{	// pass a bound argument
-		return std::forward<_Cv_TiD>(_Tid);
+		static _Cv_TiD& _Fix(_Cv_TiD& _Tid, _Untuple&&)
+		{	// pass a bound argument (as an lvalue, [func.bind.bind]/10)
+		return (_Tid);
 		}
 	};
 
@@ -873,7 +873,7 @@
 	-> decltype(_Invoke_ret(_Fr, _Obj, _Fix_arg(
 		_STD get<_Ix>(_Tpl), _STD move(_Ut))...))
 	{	// bind() and bind<R>() invocation
-	return (_Invoke_ret(_Fr,std::forward<_Cv_FD>(_Obj),_Fix_arg(
+	return (_Invoke_ret(_Fr, _Obj, _Fix_arg(
 		_STD get<_Ix>(_Tpl), _STD move(_Ut))...));
 	}
 
